# Phase 7.1 — Publish→Marketplace Bridge & Dead Nav Links

Two consequential gaps remain after Phase 7's storage normalization. This patch closes both.

---

## Problem 1: Publishing a bot doesn't make it discoverable

### Current behaviour

When a user publishes a bot via the 5-step wizard at `/app/marketplace/publish/[botId]`:

1. `handlePublish()` creates a `PublishedPreset` object (with `cloneGraph(bot.graph)` — correct).
2. `publishPreset(preset)` pushes it into `state.publishedPresets`.
3. The user is redirected to `/app/creator/dashboard`, which reads `state.publishedPresets` — so the creator **can** see their own listing. ✓

But the actual browsable marketplace pages — both `/app/marketplace` (logged-in) and `/marketplace` (public, logged-out) — read exclusively from the **static** `MARKETPLACE_PRESETS` array imported from `mock/data.ts`. They never consult `state.publishedPresets`.

**Net effect**: A published strategy is permanently invisible to every other user. Nobody can discover or fork it through the marketplace UI. This was the exact fidelity concern flagged in the original Phase 7 spec.

### Current behaviour (creator dashboard → "View in Market" link)

The Creator Dashboard table links each published preset to `/app/marketplace/${preset.id}`. That detail page does `MARKETPLACE_PRESETS.find(p => p.id === presetId)` — a freshly published preset won't be in that static array, so the link 404s immediately.

