## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **De-listing / unpublishing**: The publish wizard currently has no "unpublish" or "delist" action. Once published, a preset lives in the marketplace forever (in the mock data layer). Should we add a `deletePublishedPreset(id)` action that removes from both `publishedPresets` and `marketplacePresets`? I'd recommend yes — even as a stub, it keeps the data model clean. The Creator Dashboard table already has an "Actions" column where we can wire a "Delist" button.

> [!NOTE]
> **Duplicate ID guard**: If a user publishes the same bot twice, they'd get two marketplace entries. The publish action should either update the existing entry (upsert by `botId`) or prevent re-publishing. The publish wizard page could check `publishedPresets` for an existing entry and show an "Update Listing" flow instead. For now, I'd allow multiple publications (each creates a new preset ID) — this matches real marketplace behaviour where you can list multiple variations.

